<ArticleLayout
  title="Climate-Resilient Building & Renewable Energy"
  description="Rammed-earth construction, skills pathways and a renewable-energy resilience valley concept in Sierra Leone."
>
  <p>
    Buildings and energy systems shape how well a community withstands
    climate shocks. This area builds practical, locally buildable
    resilience, alongside a larger renewable-energy initiative in
    development.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    EarthBuild uses rammed-earth construction methods to deliver
    climate-resilient micro-infrastructure, paired with a genuine
    skills pathway so the construction technique itself becomes an
    ongoing livelihood.
  </p>
  <p>
    Alongside it, a larger resilience and renewable-energy valley
    concept is in development with international research and funding
    partners, aiming to connect clean energy access with the same
    local-skills logic that runs through Ayara&rsquo;s other work.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    We start with a small, provable pilot and document its results
    honestly before scaling. EarthBuild&rsquo;s early results inform
    how larger, capital-intensive projects like the resilience valley
    get designed and pitched to funders.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
